{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Keeping loving-kindness for thousands.</b> I mention it for his sons and his sons' sons, up to the thousandth generation, and likewise it is written: ״שומר הברית והחסד לאלף דור״. And Rashbam explains that 'for thousands' here is the same as 'for the thousandth generation' there, just as he calls the fourth generation 'fourths,' so he calls the thousandth generation 'thousands.'" "<b>Bearing iniquity.</b> For a man who sins by means of the evil inclination that compels him to sin." "<b>And transgression.</b> These are the rebellious ones — a man who sins to provoke. And thus it says: ״מלך מואב פשע בי״." "<b>And sin.</b> Inadvertent, as it says: ״נפש כי תחטא בשגגה״ — meaning, these I bear, and I do not exact payment from them immediately." "<b>And will by no means clear.</b> That He does not clear them completely, except by means of repentance and good deeds. And likewise the Sages said: 'and will clear' — for those who return; and He does not clear those who do not return, but rather visits the iniquity of the fathers upon the children etc." "<b>Visits.</b> This too is from the measure of His mercy, may the Holy One, blessed be He, that He does not hasten to exact punishment but waits until the day of reckoning, as it is written: וביום פקדי. Yet it is not from among the thirteen attributes, and this is difficult according to the one who says that וימהר משה was because he feared lest He add onto the fourth generation — but on the contrary, according to what was explained, this is a measure of mercy, that He does not pay a man according to his deed."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:44.465054713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}